Package: nightmodecontroller-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Thomas Martin <tmmuttathara@gmail.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1
Recommends: i2c-tools
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/prompt-smithy/nightModeController_Linux
Description: Tray app for external-display brightness and scheduled colour temperature
 Night Mode Controller drives external-monitor brightness over DDC/CI and
 follows a morning/evening colour-temperature schedule. It lives in the
 system tray with per-channel popups, scroll-to-adjust with OSD feedback,
 a settings window, and a full command-line interface.
 .
 DDC/CI brightness needs i2c access: install i2c-tools, join the i2c group
 (sudo usermod -aG i2c $USER), and log out and back in.
